From cd1dd20740e492dc0ee9ec0adff0bf42bde3664a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kostiantyn Andriiuk <konstantin@andriyuk.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 18:32:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] usb: xhci: keep onclite reset at primary stop

Keep controlled xHCI logical-death cleanup before shared-HCD removal, but
defer the DWC3 physical reset to the existing primary-HCD stop callback.
This isolates whether the early reset caused the long primary xhci_stop()
MMIO stall seen with a loaded RTL8152 hub on v11.

Signed-off-by: Kostiantyn Andriiuk <konstantin@andriyuk.com>
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
index 326fa7546..02b7cd13c 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
@@ -483,7 +483,6 @@ void xhci_plat_remove(struct platform_device *dev)
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&xhci->lock, flags);
 		dev_info(&dev->dev,
 			 "[onclite-usb-v11] pending xHCI work completed\n");
-		xhci_priv_plat_stop(hcd);
 	}
 
 	if (shared_hcd) {
-- 
2.43.0

